## CASE NARRATIVE

A 45-year-old female presented with rash, pruritus (itching), nausea and dizziness. The patient had been taking amoxicillin, started 5 days prior to reporting, along with paracetamol taken as needed. Reaction onset occurred approximately 3 days after starting amoxicillin and symptoms were ongoing (not recovered) as of the day of reporting.

## CONCLUSION

Amoxicillin is the suspected drug associated with the reported rash, pruritus, nausea and dizziness. Based on the available information, the WHO-UMC causality assessment is POSSIBLE.
